{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"STOP BEFORE IMPLEMENTING: the corrected defect is ALREADY FIXED on current origin/main. Recommending we do NOT apply the planned change.\n\n## The two timeouts ran against a workflow that no longer exists\n\nBoth timed-out runs used main at the time of dispatch, not the patchset, for the reusable workflow:\n\n| Run | main at dispatch | mutation jobs | outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 31560638673 | 57d19254 | 1 job, no matrix suffix | cancelled at 30m16s |\n| 31562494026 | 2c0fec01 | 1 job, no matrix suffix | cancelled at 30m17s |\n\n57d19254 is 'ci: establish mutation gate walking skeleton' — a SINGLE 'bounded mutation gate' job that ran every selected shard serially under one timeout-minutes: 30. That is why all-shards blew the budget, and it is the shape the ticket's proof describes.\n\nCommit ac0f62be11 'Complete phased mutation gate core' landed on main at 2026-08-12 03:35 UTC and replaced it with a selector job plus a per-shard parallel matrix: 'matrix: {shard: selected_shards}', so each shard is now its own job with its OWN 30-minute budget.\n\n## The all-shards case now passes\n\nRun 31563668309 (main at ac0f62be) selected ALL 7 shards. Every one succeeded:\n\n| shard | duration |\n|---|---|\n| push-policy | 0m39s |\n| compact-policy | 0m41s |\n| validate | 6m04s |\n| next-batch | 7m25s |\n| signing | 13m09s |\n| gates | 11m25s |\n| reducer-processors | 20m22s |\n\nWorst shard 20m22s against a 30m budget — about 32% headroom. This is precisely AC4's reproduction scenario (a change touching a global_support path selecting all 7) and it completes cleanly, so AC1 is already satisfied.\n\n## Why I did not apply the planned fix\n\n1. Dropping .github/workflows/test.yml from global_support would REDUCE gate coverage to solve a problem that no longer exists. The over-broad selection is real but it is no longer harmful now that shards run in parallel — it costs runner slots, not a red vote.\n2. Raising timeout-minutes is unnecessary: no shard job on the new workflow has come close to 30m. Raising it now would be tuning against a number measured on the retired serial workflow.\n3. The self-blocking concern in AC5 dissolves with it: a change touching mutation-shards.toml selects all 7 shards, and all 7 now pass.\n\n## What is actually blocking change 1615\n\n1615's runs were dispatched while main was still at the walking-skeleton commit. It needs a REBASE onto current origin/main (de267b06, which contains ac0f62be) so its Verified run picks up the parallel matrix — the standard 'pre-analysis failure -> rebase, never recheck' path. No repository change is needed for it.\n\n## Residual work worth keeping\n\nAC3 stands on its own merit and is independent of all the above: a timed-out or cancelled mutation job still aggregates into a bare 'CANCELLED:' Verified -1 that carries no test signal. That is defence-in-depth against the next timeout, whatever causes it, and is the only part of this ticket I would still implement.\n\nSeparately, the 'select mutation shards' STEP failed outright on runs 31563192064 and 31563305610 (both on ac0f62be). I could not read the logs — the runs were still in progress — so I am flagging it as unverified rather than diagnosing it. If it reproduces it deserves its own ticket."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786511107876781001,"uuid":"0dbeb1b3-5f75-402f-adba-3325036b7d4f"}